{
    "info": {
        "_postman_id": "school-incidents-v1",
        "name": "School Management — Incident Triggers",
        "description": "One request per incident in rca_eval_dataset.jsonl (school-001 … school-015).\nEach request sets X-Incident-ID so the IncidentIdFilter logs incidentId into MDC,\nenabling the RCA-Agent to match ground-truth evaluation metrics for every RCA run.\n\nPre-requisites:\n• Import MTech-Project.postman_environment.json and select it.\n• School service running on {{school_base}} (default http://localhost:8081).\n• The collection-level pre-request script logs in as admin@school.edu and caches the\n  JWT in the 'school_token' collection variable for the duration of the run.\n• school-013 needs a student token — set 'school_student_token' manually OR run the\n  school-004 register request first and log in as the new student to capture it.",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
    },
    "variable": [
        {
            "key": "school_base",
            "value": "http://localhost:8081",
            "type": "string"
        },
        {
            "key": "incidentId",
            "value": "",
            "type": "string"
        },
        {
            "key": "school_token",
            "value": "",
            "type": "string"
        },
        {
            "key": "school_refresh_token",
            "value": "",
            "type": "string"
        },
        {
            "key": "school_student_token",
            "value": "",
            "type": "string"
        }
    ],
    "event": [
        {
            "listen": "prerequest",
            "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                    "// Collection-level pre-request: obtain an admin JWT if not already cached.",
                    "var token = pm.collectionVariables.get('school_token');",
                    "if (!token || token === '') {",
                    "    var base = pm.collectionVariables.get('school_base') || 'http://localhost:8081';",
                    "    pm.sendRequest({",
                    "        url: base + '/api/v1/auth/login',",
                    "        method: 'POST',",
                    "        header: [{ key: 'Content-Type', value: 'application/json' }],",
                    "        body: {",
                    "            mode: 'raw',",
                    "            raw: JSON.stringify({",
                    "                usernameOrEmail: 'admin@school.edu',",
                    "                password: 'Admin@1234'",
                    "            })",
                    "        }",
                    "    }, function(err, res) {",
                    "        if (!err && res.code === 200) {",
                    "            var json = res.json();",
                    "            if (json.data && json.data.accessToken) {",
                    "                pm.collectionVariables.set('school_token', json.data.accessToken);",
                    "                pm.collectionVariables.set('school_refresh_token', json.data.refreshToken || '');",
                    "            }",
                    "        }",
                    "    });",
                    "}"
                ]
            }
        }
    ],
    "item": [
        {
            "name": "auth-service",
            "description": "Incidents whose service_name is auth-service.",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "school-001 | JwtAuthFilter NPE on malformed Bearer token",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "prerequest",
                            "script": {
                                "type": "text/javascript",
                                "exec": [
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('incidentId', 'school-001');",
                                    "// Deliberately set a malformed token that has no subject claim.",
                                    "// The JwtAuthenticationFilter calls getUserId() on a null Claims object.",
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('malformed_token', 'malformed_token_without_subject');"
                                ]
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Authorization",
                                "value": "Bearer malformed_token_without_subject"
                            },
                            {
                                "key": "X-Incident-ID",
                                "value": "{{incidentId}}"
                            }
                        ],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{school_base}}/api/users/me",
                            "host": [
                                "{{school_base}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "users",
                                "me"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Triggers: JwtAuthenticationFilter.doFilterInternal calls claims.getSubject() on null — NPE.\nThe 'Authorization: Bearer malformed_token_without_subject' header contains a JWT that\ncannot be parsed so claims is null. IncidentIdFilter runs before security, so incidentId=school-001\nis always logged even when the request is rejected.\nClass: null-reference | Difficulty: easy | Split: train"
                    },
                    "response": []
                },
                {
                    "name": "school-003 | Refresh Token Reuse After Single-Use (Token Replay)",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "prerequest",
                            "script": {
                                "type": "text/javascript",
                                "exec": [
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('incidentId', 'school-003');"
                                ]
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            },
                            {
                                "key": "X-Incident-ID",
                                "value": "{{incidentId}}"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"d3c9f1a2-7e4b-4c88-a1d2-3f9e8b7c6d5a\"\n}",
                            "options": {
                                "raw": {
                                    "language": "json"
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{school_base}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
                            "host": [
                                "{{school_base}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "auth",
                                "refresh"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Triggers: refreshToken endpoint does not invalidate the old token after issuing a new one.\nSend this request twice with the same refreshToken to confirm both succeed.\nClass: token-replay | Difficulty: medium | Split: train"
                    },
                    "response": []
                },
                {
                    "name": "school-004 | Register — NPE When Email Already Exists",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "prerequest",
                            "script": {
                                "type": "text/javascript",
                                "exec": [
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('incidentId', 'school-004');"
                                ]
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            },
                            {
                                "key": "X-Incident-ID",
                                "value": "{{incidentId}}"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"jane.doe\",\n  \"email\": \"jane.doe@school.edu\",\n  \"password\": \"Password@123\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Jane\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Doe\"\n}",
                            "options": {
                                "raw": {
                                    "language": "json"
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{school_base}}/api/v1/auth/register",
                            "host": [
                                "{{school_base}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "auth",
                                "register"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Triggers: register calls user.getEmail().toLowerCase() without checking existsByEmail first.\nSend ONCE to register. Send AGAIN (same email) to trigger the NPE on duplicate.\nClass: null-reference | Difficulty: medium | Split: train"
                    },
                    "response": []
                },
                {
                    "name": "school-007 | Refresh Token — Concurrent Reuse Race Condition",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "prerequest",
                            "script": {
                                "type": "text/javascript",
                                "exec": [
                                    "pm.collectionVariables.set('incidentId', 'school-007');",
                                    "// This incident is the concurrent variant of school-003.",
                                    "// Use Postman Runner with 3 iterations all hitting the same refreshToken."
                                ]
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            {
                                "key": "Content-Type",
                                "value": "application/json"
                            },
                            {
                                "key": "X-Incident-ID",
                                "value": "{{incidentId}}"
                            }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"d3c9f1a2-7e4b-4c88-a1d2-3f9e8b7c6d5a\"\n}",
                            "options": {
                                "raw": {
                                    "language": "json"
                                }
                            }
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{school_base}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
                            "host": [
                                "{{school_base}}"
                            ],
                            "path": [
                                "api",
                                "v1",
                                "auth",
                                "refresh"
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Triggers: Concurrent refresh requests with the same token pass the isValid() check before either marks it used.\nUse Postman Collection Runner with Iterations=3 and Delay=0 to reproduce the race.\nClass: race-condition | Difficulty: hard | Split: train"
                    },
                    "response": []
                },
